      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "Softmax exponentials can be stabilized by subtracting the largest logit. For a first chunk with logits two and one, the maximum is two and the scaled exponential sum is one plus e to the minus one, about one point three seven.\n",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 15.448,
          "duration": 15.048,
          "until": 15.998000000000001
        },
        {
          "say": "The next chunk contains four and zero, so the running maximum rises to four. Rescale the earlier sum by e to the minus two, then add the new exponentials: one plus e to the minus four. The combined result is about one point two zero.\n",
          "start": 15.998000000000001,
          "end": 31.910000000000004,
          "duration": 15.912,
          "until": 32.61
        },
        {
          "say": "The state carries both the maximum and a rescaled sum. The update keeps the denominator equivalent to processing all four logits together, while avoiding a direct exponential of a large value.\n",
          "start": 32.61,
          "end": 44.778,
          "duration": 12.168,
          "until": 45.328
        }
